From: xuxh1 <18172956238@163.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 13:36:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(hydrology): routing takes floodplain re-infiltration
 where the soil saw the flood (Q-47)

DEF_FLOODPLAIN_INFILT_FIX (default off; acts only with DEF_FLOODPLAIN_INFILTRATION). The routing now keeps, at each publish, the flood water offered per input cell, per unit catchment and per patch. A patch's re-infiltration goes to its input cells in proportion to the flood water it was offered there, and a cell's share to its unit catchments in proportion to their flood water in it, instead of both by area. The part a unit catchment cannot give at a routing step stays in acc_inf_uc for the next step instead of being dropped; acc_inf_uc moves to MOD_Grid_RiverLakeTimeVars and, with the fix, goes into the routing restart (old restarts read as zero). The yearly C-44/Q-43 log line adds the amount still owed at the end of the year. With the key off, the accumulation, deduction, publish and log follow the old code paths.

---
 main/HYDRO/MOD_Grid_RiverLakeFlow.F90     | 183 +++++++++++++++++++---
 main/HYDRO/MOD_Grid_RiverLakeTimeVars.F90 |  44 +++++-
 share/MOD_Namelist.F90                    |   6 +
 3 files changed, 209 insertions(+), 24 deletions(-)

